menu "KVMpad HID core (TASK-050)"

    config KVM_HID_BENCH_PROBE
        bool "Bench only: `hid probe` console command (wire checks from the HOST side)"
        default n
        help
            Adds `hid probe <keys|rollover|move|chords>` to the UART console. Each probe is a fixed sequence that
            enters the normal LOCAL path (typed intents -> InputArbiter -> HidScheduler), so the HOST-side capture
            script test/hil/hid_capture_windows.py can check what really arrives on the wire (AT-HID-02/03/04/06/08,
            AT-KEY-07). keys / rollover / move are harmless: F13..F24 only (no default action on a desktop) and
            mouse moves that return to the start point, never a click or a Consumer usage. `chords` acts on the
            HOST desktop (Alt+Tab and Win+D twice each, Ctrl+Shift+Esc, then an Alt+Tab cut by RELEASE_ALL; never
            Ctrl+Alt+Del) and is run only with the owner's go-ahead. The probe runs only while the HOST is
            mounted and nobody else owns the input; it ends with RELEASE_ALL. Never enable it in a release build.

endmenu
